        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (service_name, pool_name) (db_client_connection_pending_requests{service_name=~\"$service\"})",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}} / {{pool_name}}"
        }
      ],
      "pluginVersion": "13.0.3",
      "description": "**The most important number in the stack** (§5.3). When the API gets slow under load the cause is almost never \"the code is slow\" — it is that all 10 pool connections are checked out and 400 requests are queueing for one. Utilisation looks *fine* at 100%; saturation is what reveals it, and it moves before latency does.\n\nAnything sustained above 0 is a finding. Above 20 is the `DBPoolExhausted` page (`observability/prometheus/rules/operational.yaml`).",
      "id": 8,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      }
